hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16130","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, he said: Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Aslami narrated to me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put him in command of a detachment, so I went out in it, and he said: If you seize so-and-so, burn him with fire. When I turned, he called me and said: If you seize him, kill him, for none punishes with fire except the Lord of fire."
"16131","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ziyad, meaning Ibn Sad, informed me that Abu al-Zinad said: Hanzalah ibn Ali informed me, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, the companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and a group with him to a man from Udhrah, and said: If you gain power over so-and-so, burn him with fire. So they set out until, when they were hidden from him, he called them or sent after them, and they were brought back, then said: If you gain power over him, kill him and do not burn him with fire, for only the Lord of fire punishes with fire."
"16132","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ziyad informed us that Abu al-Zinad informed him, he said: Hanzalah ibn Ali al-Aslami informed me that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, the companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and a group with him as a detachment to a man, and he mentioned its meaning."
"16133","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting in travel, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"16134","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, that he saw a man on a camel following the peoples baggage at Mina, while the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present, and the man says: Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking. Qatadah said: It was mentioned to us that that caller was Bilal."
"16135","He said: Attab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah and Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hamzah informed me that he heard his father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, on the back of every camel is a devil, so when you ride them, mention Allah Almighty, then do not fall short of your needs."
